Hi Harald,

At Fri, 24 Jun 2005 18:59:08 +0200,
Harald Welte wrote:
> 
> Hi!
> 
> I've recently obtained a Turion64 notebook (branded as TARGA, originally
> built by MSI).  It is based on ATI chipset (SB400)
> 
> However, I don't get any audio output, neither on the headphone jack nor
> on the speakers - despite everything looking quite nice in /proc/asound
> (see remainder of mail).  I've already tried ac97 quirks and played with
> every possible mixer setting.  No success :(
> 
> I'm happy to any suggestions and/or hints where to start further
> debugging the issue.

After a quick look at your information, I couldn't find anything
wrong.  The ac97 register values look OK (compared with ALC658
datasheet).

Just to be sure, could you install alsa-driver-1.0.9b?
Also, please attach /etc/asound.state (after "alsactl store") to check
the mixer configuration.

There have been some bug reports with ATIIXP-laptop, and interestingly
someone reported that it was fixed by disabling ACPI.  But, his case
was only for the speaker output, so not 100% identical with your
case.


Takashi


